    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Read Config and Google Sheets Data\n\nFirst, open the **Config** node and paste your Google Sheet ID. You can find it in your Google Sheet URL, just after `/d/`.\n\nThen, select your Google account credentials in each Google Sheets node.\n\nAll 4 read nodes are set to **Execute Once**, so each node will run only one time.",
        "height": 332,
        "width": 812,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "20a318a9-89e4-4f19-9b49-79c23db9ee8b",
      "name": "Sticky 11",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        304
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Create Search Queries\n\nThis step creates search queries using all cities and keywords where `Active = Yes`, along with 4 search patterns.\n\nYou can choose the search mode from `Run_Config > Opening_Mode`. The options are **Upcoming**, **Recently Opened**, or **Both**.\n\nIt also checks for duplicates. So, if you run the workflow again in the same week, it will not create the same `Search_ID` again.",
        "height": 332,
        "width": 792,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "463c97c5-7fc5-4f04-b34d-2a8c10b29d02",
      "name": "Sticky 12",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1072,
        304
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Save Tasks\n\nAll new search tasks are added to the `Search_Queue` tab with the status **Pending**.\n\nOnce this is done, we can move to **Workflow 2**.",
        "height": 332,
        "width": 252,
